 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Stability",
 "statement": "Weakly étale morphisms [sk-def-pe-morphisms] are stable under base change and\ncomposition, and the property is local on source and target for the Zariski topology.\nEvery $X$-morphism between two weakly étale $X$-schemes is weakly étale. Affine pro-étale\nmorphisms are stable under affine base change and composition.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-proetale-coefficients/sk-lem-pe-weakly-etale-stability/_section.md",
  "place": "node sk-lem-pe-weakly-etale-stability, order 702",
  "external": [
   {
    "document": "Stacks Project",
    "place": "Tag 092A"
   }
  ]
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "sk-def-pe-morphisms"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Base change preserves flatness of a morphism and its diagonal. For a composite\n$V\\to U\\to X$, the diagonal factors through $V\\times_UV\\to V\\times_XV$, which is a base\nchange of $\\Delta_{U/X}$; this gives the assertion about composites.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "For an $X$-map $h\\colon U\\to V$, the graph $U\\to U\\times_XV$ is a base change of the flat\ndiagonal of $V/X$, and the projection $U\\times_XV\\to V$ is flat because $U/X$ is flat.\nTheir composite is $h$, while $\\Delta_h$ is a base change of $\\Delta_{U/X}$. Zariski\nlocality follows from locality of flatness.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "For ind-étale rings, tensor products commute with filtered colimits, and finite\npresentation lets one choose a finite stage for each étale algebra; this gives base change\nand transitivity. The same arguments show that a filtered colimit of étale algebras has\nflat multiplication map (Stacks, Tag 092A). The ring-theoretic statements are\n[lem-weil-pbc-ind-etale-stability]; the statement about $X$-morphisms between weakly étale\nobjects is [lem-trf-weakly-etale-between-objects].",
   "uses": [
    "lem-weil-pbc-ind-etale-stability",
    "lem-trf-weakly-etale-between-objects"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "lem-weil-pbc-ind-etale-stability",
  "lem-trf-weakly-etale-between-objects"
 ],
